    "science": {
      "type": "ptm-science",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "The science behind the ritual",
        "intro": "Every PRANA formula follows the same path, from what Ayurveda observed to what our customers see in the mirror.",
        "formula_title": "The full formula",
        "formula_subtitle": "17 ingredients, with the amount and job of each",
        "col_ingredient": "Ingredient",
        "col_job": "What it does",
        "col_amount": "Amount",
        "formula_note": "Ranges as declared on our manufacturer's safety data sheet."
      },
      "blocks": {
        "step_1": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "numeral": "I",
            "title": "The ritual",
            "question": "What Ayurveda says",
            "text": "<p>Ayurveda groups turmeric with the <em>varnya</em> herbs, those used to bring clarity and radiance to the complexion. Sandalwood, or <em>chandana</em>, is a cooling herb for skin that runs hot and red. Clay was used to purify. Mixed into a paste called ubtan, the three became the haldi ritual brides still follow before their weddings.</p>",
            "link_text": "See the bridal ritual",
            "link_url": "#bridal"
          }
        },
        "step_2": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "numeral": "II",
            "title": "The formula",
            "question": "What we formulated",
            "text": "<p>Twenty versions over two years led to a smooth, pink clay cream with a skin-friendly pH of 5.0 to 7.0. Kaolin leads the clays, with bentonite and French pink clay behind it. Turmeric, sandalwood, rose and rosehip oil sit at up to 1% each, the range where botanical oils are typically used on the face. Glycerin and a coconut-derived emollient keep the mask from drying skin as it sets.</p>",
            "link_text": "See the full formula",
            "link_url": "#formula"
          }
        },
        "step_3": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "numeral": "III",
            "title": "The evidence",
            "question": "What we tested",
            "text": "<p>Fifty people aged 18 to 55, across skin tones and types, used the mask at home once or twice a week for four weeks. 91% said their skin looked clearer, brighter and more even; 93% said it felt softer and less congested. Before that, our manufacturer's safety data sheet confirmed the formula is non-toxic, non-hazardous, stable and pH 5.0 to 7.0.</p>",
            "link_text": "See all the results",
            "link_url": "#results"
          }
        },
        "step_4": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "numeral": "IV",
            "title": "The experience",
            "question": "What customers reported",
            "text": "<p>The best evidence of how a mask feels is what the people using it say. Every review below comes from a verified buyer, shown as written, including the ones that aren't five stars.</p>",
            "link_text": "Read verified reviews",
            "link_url": "#reviews"
          }
        },
        "row_1": {
          "type": "formula_row",
          "settings": {
            "ingredient": "Water",
            "job": "Creamy base so the clays spread in an even layer",
            "amount": "55–60%"
          }
        },
        "row_2": {
          "type": "formula_row",
          "settings": {
